From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 07:47:41 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 07/45] Plutonium: browser tabs as SurfaceEmbed elements, DRM
 mouse wheel

- PlutoniumTabs registry: browser-owned WebContents shown in the shell
  page with <embed type="application/x-chromium-surface-embed">. Tabs a
  page opens inherit the opener's tag; gesture-less popups are blocked;
  dialogs are surfaced to the shell; hidden tabs stay parked under the
  shell window so they paint and can be snapshotted.
- Window broker: getTabs, createTab, navigateTab, tabCommand,
  answerTabDialog, snapshotTab and tab events (shell document only).
- SurfaceEmbedHost bound for the shell document; the renderer creates the
  plugin only in main frames of the shell origin. Tabs are never the
  shell, even at the shell's URL.
- evdev: REL_WHEEL/REL_HWHEEL (and hi-res) become wheel events in
  EventConverterEvdevImpl, which non-device builds use for mice.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
